# tools/u/upstream_shape_witness.rish -- read the ordering remote's shape before rebasing onto it.
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/u/upstream_shape_witness.rish
#
# WHAT IT STANDS OVER. tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh, which reads HEAD against the anointed
# ordering remote and names the shape it finds: up_to_date, fast_forward, ahead, diverged, or the
# one that refuses -- rewritten, meaning the two share no common ancestor at all.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The sync rota seated on 20260825.210819 opens every round with
# `git pull --rebase xykj61 main`, and all fifteen of its sentences assume the piers share a
# history. On 20260825 the macOS bench spent the banked deep debride -- a collaborator's name out
# of the tree, the logs, and every commit -- and force-pushed the rewritten history to the
# ordering remote. The next round on this pier met an upstream with 3,469 commits, a local HEAD
# with 3,467, and no merge base between them. That is REDS %243, and the rota had no reading for it.
#
# WHAT THE PROOF LEGS SHOW, and why there are three. Against a rewritten upstream `git pull
# --rebase` behaves two entirely different ways, and the difference is a reflog rather than
# anything visible in the tree. The same pen, the same rewrite, the same command:
#
#   reflog present -> --fork-point finds the pre-rewrite position, 7 owned commits replay, tree clean
#   reflog absent  -> no fork point, all 15 local commits replay, the debrided name back on disk
#
# A fifth leg proves the refusal does not fire where it must not: a shallow clone outrun by its
# upstream also has an empty merge base, and reads as `shallow_repository` rather than a rewrite.
#
# A reflog is not a durable thing. Git expires it at ninety days by default, and a fresh clone has
# none at all, so the quiet path is the one that cannot be relied on.
say "upstream-shape: Language EN -- the shape of the remote, read before a rebase acts on it."
say "upstream-shape: Style Gauge Meter -- every verdict named, every count measured."
say "upstream-shape: Lens TAME -- safety first; a refusal proven only one way is not proven."

# THE LIVE READING. This pier's own shape against its ordering remote. It passes on every ordinary
# shape and on a pier that has not fetched; it refuses only on `rewritten`, which is the one
# reading a rebase must never act on unexamined.
let live = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh"]
say live.out
assert live.ok else "upstream-shape: this pier shares no ancestor with its ordering remote -- rebase --onto before working"
assert live.out contains "verdict=" else "upstream-shape: want a verdict named"

# THE CRUX, reproduced on metal rather than argued. Two real repositories, a real filter-branch
# rewrite, the reflog removed the way ninety days removes it -- then the pull itself, and the
# debrided name measured back in the working tree.
let gone = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh" "prove-rewritten"]
say gone.out
assert gone.ok else "upstream-shape: the reflog-absent proof must exit 0"
assert gone.out contains "reflog_entries=0" else "upstream-shape: want the reflog actually gone"
assert gone.out contains "fork_point=absent" else "upstream-shape: want no fork point computable"
assert gone.out contains "replay_count=15" else "upstream-shape: want all fifteen local commits queued for replay"
assert gone.out contains "verdict=rewritten" else "upstream-shape: want the refusal named"
assert gone.out contains "name_residue_after_pull=1" else "upstream-shape: want the debrided name proven back on disk"

# THE QUIET PATH, proven beside it. Same pen, same rewrite, reflog intact: seven owned commits
# replay and nothing comes back. Without this leg the fault above could be read as a property of
# rewriting rather than of the reflog, and the repair would aim at the wrong thing.
let kept = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh" "prove-forkpoint"]
say kept.out
assert kept.ok else "upstream-shape: the reflog-present proof must exit 0"
assert kept.out contains "reflog_entries=1" else "upstream-shape: want the reflog present"
assert kept.out contains "replay_count=7" else "upstream-shape: want only this pier's own commits replayed"
assert kept.out contains "name_residue_after_pull=0" else "upstream-shape: want a clean tree on the fork-point path"

# THE OTHER SIDE OF THE REFUSAL. A wall that fires on ordinary work is a wall somebody turns off,
# so an ordinary shared divergence is proven to pass as hard as a rewrite is proven to refuse.
let ord = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh" "prove-ordinary"]
say ord.out
assert ord.ok else "upstream-shape: an ordinary divergence must pass"
assert ord.out contains "verdict=diverged" else "upstream-shape: want an ordinary divergence named as such"

# THE FALSE POSITIVE, proven not to fire. A shallow clone outrun by its upstream also has no merge
# base, and without a reading of its own it would be told its remote had been rewritten -- a
# refusal on ordinary work, which is the shape of a wall people disable. A depth-1 clone that has
# NOT been outrun still finds its base, so the pen walks the upstream past the boundary first;
# that was measured before it was written down.
let shallow = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh" "prove-shallow"]
say shallow.out
assert shallow.ok else "upstream-shape: a shallow clone must not read as rewritten"
assert shallow.out contains "is_shallow=true" else "upstream-shape: want the pen actually shallow"
assert shallow.out contains "merge_base_found=0" else "upstream-shape: want the empty merge base reproduced"
assert shallow.out contains "verdict=shallow_repository" else "upstream-shape: want the shallow shape named apart from a rewrite"

# A PIER THAT HAS NOT FETCHED reports a machine fact and passes. A guard that reds on a missing
# network stops a line for something no tree could repair.
let unfetched = run ["sh" "-c" "UPSTREAM_SHAPE_REMOTE=no-such-remote sh tools/fixtures/upstream_shape_scan.sh"]
assert unfetched.ok else "upstream-shape: an unfetched remote is a machine fact, never a tree red"
assert unfetched.out contains "verdict=no_remote_ref" else "upstream-shape: want the unfetched shape named"

say "GREEN: upstream-shape -- the live shape read, the reflog-absent replay of all fifteen commits reproduced with the debrided name back on disk, the fork-point path proven clean at seven, an ordinary divergence and an outrun shallow clone both proven to pass, and an unfetched remote read as a machine fact"
